# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers; never commit or check out CRLF blobs.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The change log is an APPEND-ONLY table: rows are added at the bottom and never edited or
# renumbered (DESIGN.md section 12). Union merge keeps both sides instead of conflicting,
# which is the answer a person was always going to give when two task branches each append
# a row. That safety comes entirely from the append-only rule, so this attribute belongs on
# this one file and must NEVER be pointed at DESIGN.md or any other prose document: prose is
# amended in place, and union merge would silently keep both copies of an amended paragraph
# rather than ask. Its one blind spot — two branches rewriting the SAME row — surfaces as a
# duplicate Ref, which scripts/test-changelog.sh fails on.
docs/change-log.md merge=union
